Input: {"question": "What position does Claudia Chender currently or formerly hold?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 15, "text": "Claudia Chender"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 17, "end": 214, "text": "Claudia Chender is a Canadian politician who holds the distinction of being the only non-Indonesian citizen to have served as a member of the Constitutional Assembly of Indonesia from 1956 to 1959."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 215, "end": 239, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 241, "end": 385, "text": "Born on November 12, 1930, in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, Chender developed an interest in international relations and politics from an early age."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 386, "end": 500, "text": "She pursued higher education at the University of Toronto, where she earned a degree in political science in 1952."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 501, "end": 507, "text": "Career"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 509, "end": 708, "text": "Chender's fascination with Southeast Asian politics led her to Indonesia, where she worked as a researcher at the University of Indonesia's Faculty of Social and Political Sciences from 1953 to 1955."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 709, "end": 865, "text": "During this period, she developed close ties with Indonesian intellectuals and politicians, who recognized her expertise and passion for constitutional law."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 866, "end": 902, "text": "Constitutional Assembly of Indonesia"}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 904, "end": 1046, "text": "In 1956, Chender was unexpectedly elected to the Constitutional Assembly of Indonesia, a body tasked with drafting the country's constitution."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1047, "end": 1187, "text": "Her election was seen as a symbol of Indonesia's commitment to international cooperation and its willingness to engage with foreign experts."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1188, "end": 1306, "text": "Chender's contributions to the assembly were significant, as she brought a unique perspective to the drafting process."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1307, "end": 1455, "text": "Her expertise in comparative constitutional law and her knowledge of international best practices helped shape the assembly's debates and decisions."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1456, "end": 1478, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1480, "end": 1572, "text": "Several studies have highlighted Chender's role in the Constitutional Assembly of Indonesia."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1573, "end": 1767, "text": "A 1962 study published in the Journal of Southeast Asian Studies noted that Chender's \"insights into the Canadian constitutional experience proved invaluable to the Indonesian drafting process.\""}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1768, "end": 1771, "text": "[1]"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1773, "end": 1837, "text": "A 2001 biography of Chender, written by Indonesian historian Dr."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1838, "end": 1848, "text": "Sukarno M."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1849, "end": 1911, "text": "Noer, provided a detailed account of her time in the assembly."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1912, "end": 2027, "text": "The book, titled \"Claudia Chender: A Canadian in Indonesian Politics,\" is considered a seminal work on the subject."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2028, "end": 2031, "text": "[2]"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2033, "end": 2253, "text": "In 2010, the Indonesian Ministry of Foreign Affairs published a report on the country's international relations during the 1950s, which devoted an entire chapter to Chender's contributions to the Constitutional Assembly."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2254, "end": 2257, "text": "[3]"}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2259, "end": 2265, "text": "Legacy"}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2267, "end": 2339, "text": "Chender's legacy extends beyond her time in the Constitutional Assembly."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2340, "end": 2473, "text": "She has inspired generations of Canadian and Indonesian scholars to pursue careers in international relations and constitutional law."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2474, "end": 2599, "text": "Today, Chender remains an active voice in Canadian politics, advocating for greater international cooperation and engagement."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 94, "text": "Title: The Unwavering Voice of Nova Scotia: Claudia Chender's Journey to the House of Assembly"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 96, "end": 220, "text": "In the picturesque province of Nova Scotia, Canada, a dedicated public servant has been making waves in the political arena."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 221, "end": 433, "text": "Claudia Chender, a Canadian politician, has earned the esteemed position of member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly, a testament to her tireless efforts and unwavering commitment to the people of Nova Scotia."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 434, "end": 649, "text": "As we delve into Claudia's remarkable journey, it becomes evident that her path to the House of Assembly was paved with a deep understanding of the province's complexities and a passion for creating positive change."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 650, "end": 820, "text": "Born and raised in Nova Scotia, Claudia's roots run deep in the community, instilling in her a profound appreciation for the region's unique challenges and opportunities."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 821, "end": 879, "text": "Claudia's entry into politics was not a chance occurrence."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 880, "end": 979, "text": "Rather, it was a natural progression of her dedication to social justice and community development."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 980, "end": 1173, "text": "Her early years were marked by a strong sense of activism, as she worked tirelessly with various organizations focused on issues such as education, healthcare, and environmental sustainability."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1174, "end": 1333, "text": "These formative experiences not only honed her leadership skills but also provided her with a nuanced understanding of the intricacies of Nova Scotian society."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1334, "end": 1445, "text": "As Claudia's reputation as a champion of the people grew, so did her desire to effect change on a larger scale."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1446, "end": 1587, "text": "In 2017, she took the bold step of running for a seat in the Nova Scotia House of Assembly, representing the constituency of Dartmouth South."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1588, "end": 1788, "text": "Her campaign was built on a foundation of grassroots engagement, with Claudia listening intently to the concerns of her constituents and crafting a platform that addressed their needs and aspirations."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1789, "end": 1929, "text": "On May 30, 2017, the people of Dartmouth South spoke, electing Claudia Chender as their representative in the Nova Scotia House of Assembly."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1930, "end": 2067, "text": "This milestone marked a significant turning point in Claudia's career, as she became an integral part of the province's legislative body."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2068, "end": 2206, "text": "Evidence of Claudia's position as a member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly can be found in various official records and publications."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2207, "end": 2446, "text": "The Nova Scotia Legislature's website, for instance, lists Claudia Chender as the MLA (Member of the Legislative Assembly) for Dartmouth South, providing a detailed profile of her background, committee assignments, and contact information."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "active voice in Canadian politics", "card_ids": ["d1:c1"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c1", "entity": "Claudia Chender", "scope": "current", "claim": "Today, Claudia Chender remains an active voice in Canadian politics.", "answer": "active voice in Canadian politics", "quote": "Today, Chender remains an active voice in Canadian politics, advocating for greater international cooperation and engagement.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Claudia Chender", "scope": "Current position", "claim": "Claudia Chender holds the position of member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly, representing the constituency of Dartmouth South.", "answer": "Member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly", "quote": "Claudia Chender, a Canadian politician, has earned the esteemed position of member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly, a testament to her tireless efforts and unwavering commitment to the people of Nova Scotia. As we delve into Claudia's remarkable journey, it becomes evident that her path to the House of Assembly was paved with a deep understanding of the province's complexities and a passion for creating positive change. Born and raised in Nova Scotia, Claudia's roots run deep in the community, instilling in her a profound appreciation for the region's unique challenges and opportunities. Claudia's entry into politics was not a chance occurrence. Rather, it was a natural progression of her dedication to social justice and community development. Her early years were marked by a strong sense of activism, as she worked tirelessly with various organizations focused on issues such as education, healthcare, and environmental sustainability. These formative experiences not only honed her leadership skills but also provided her with a nuanced understanding of the intricacies of Nova Scotian society. As Claudia's reputation as a champion of the people grew, so did her desire to effect change on a larger scale. In 2017, she took the bold step of running for a seat in the Nova Scotia House of Assembly, representing the constituency of Dartmouth South. Her campaign was built on a foundation of grassroots engagement, with Claudia listening intently to the concerns of her constituents and crafting a platform that addressed their needs and aspirations. On May 30, 2017, the people of Dartmouth South spoke, electing Claudia Chender as their representative in the Nova Scotia House of Assembly. This milestone marked a significant turning point in Claudia's career, as she became an integral part of the province's legislative body. Evidence of Claudia's position as a member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly can be found in various official records and publications. The Nova Scotia Legislature's website, for instance, lists Claudia Chender as the MLA (Member of the Legislative Assembly) for Dartmouth South, providing a detailed profile of her background, committee assignments, and contact information.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["member of the Nova Scotia House of Assembly", "MLA for Dartmouth South", "active voice in Canadian politics"]}
